   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Vincent,<div>You are using org.renjin.cran:RMySQL:1.0.52 ?</div><div><br></div><div>I suspect this is a consequence of our yet-unfinished efforts to migrate Renjin&#39;s S3-based database packages, which include RMySQL to be more compatible with GNU R&#39;s S4-based packages. For the time being, our RMySQL package cannot be loaded at the same time as RSQLite or the DBI package. </div><div><br></div><div>You can find more details here on this thread:</div><div><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/renjin-dev/KifD7NpqqAQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/renjin-dev/KifD7NpqqAQ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343574612000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-B3NoUeLzw2GrfAf3-HMk\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/renjin-dev/KifD7NpqqAQ</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>I expect to finish migrating the RMySQL, ROracle, and RPostgresQL packages to S4 in early 2017.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Alex</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
